      "message": "Thanks Will, good catch!\n\nBoth cases are real. In PS3, show_pte() scopes the P3S context to the mm it walks with P3S_CONTEXT_REMOTE_MM(mm), so pte_offset_map() indexes the PTE table with that mm\u0027s geometry, for init_mm under a 4KB task and for a 4KB active_mm borrowed by a kernel thread.\n\nIt also prints mm_pte_size(mm) and the new mm_va_bits(mm), so the header reads \"4k pages, 39-bit VAs\" for a 4KB mm.\n\nI checked both cases on a VM: show_pte() now prints the same PTE as a direct walk, where PS2 printed 0 or another entry.",
